window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-054.json",{"day":54,"title":"Confidence Is Not the Absence of Doubt","targetWords":[{"word":"speech","gloss":"讲话","context":"A student preparing her first public speech believed that mental strength meant never feeling uncertain.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"mental","gloss":"心理的","context":"A student preparing her first public speech believed that mental strength meant never feeling uncertain.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"dream","gloss":"梦想","context":"Her dream was to speak confidently, but practice alone often left her more anxious.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"alone","gloss":"独自","context":"Her dream was to speak confidently, but practice alone often left her more anxious.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"desire","gloss":"渴望","context":"She had a strong desire to make her parents happy and held the belief that capable people did not need advice.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"happy","gloss":"快乐的","context":"She had a strong desire to make her parents happy and held the belief that capable people did not need advice.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"belief","gloss":"信念","context":"She had a strong desire to make her parents happy and held the belief that capable people did not need advice.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"advice","gloss":"建议","context":"She had a strong desire to make her parents happy and held the belief that capable people did not need advice.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"emotion","gloss":"情绪","context":"Every uncomfortable emotion therefore seemed like a moral failure.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"moral","gloss":"道德的","context":"Every uncomfortable emotion therefore seemed like a moral failure.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"aware","gloss":"意识到的","context":"Her tutor helped her become aware of a different possibility: confidence could include doubt.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"confidence","gloss":"信心","context":"Her tutor helped her become aware of a different possibility: confidence could include doubt.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"doubt","gloss":"怀疑","context":"Her tutor helped her become aware of a different possibility: confidence could include doubt.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"smart","gloss":"聪明的","context":"A smart decision was not necessarily an immediate one, and a calm manner did not reveal how much work had occurred beneath it.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"manner","gloss":"方式","context":"A smart decision was not necessarily an immediate one, and a calm manner did not reveal how much work had occurred beneath it.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"familiar","gloss":"熟悉的","context":"The tutor asked her to begin with a familiar subject rather than demonstrate that she was intelligent through complicated language.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"intelligent","gloss":"聪明的","context":"The tutor asked her to begin with a familiar subject rather than demonstrate that she was intelligent through complicated language.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"pretty","gloss":"相当","context":"The first recording was pretty uneven, but its flaws were useful evidence.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"sensitive","gloss":"敏感的","context":"Being sensitive to feedback did not mean accepting every criticism as accurate.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"psychology","gloss":"心理学","context":"An introductory lesson in psychology showed how attention could narrow under pressure, regardless of talent.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"talent","gloss":"才能","context":"An introductory lesson in psychology showed how attention could narrow under pressure, regardless of talent.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"vision","gloss":"愿景","context":"She could maintain a long-term vision while accepting a tough rehearsal.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"tough","gloss":"艰难的","context":"She could maintain a long-term vision while accepting a tough rehearsal.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"yes","gloss":"是的","context":"When asked whether she was ready to try again, she answered yes, though she remained afraid.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"afraid","gloss":"害怕的","context":"When asked whether she was ready to try again, she answered yes, though she remained afraid.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"secret","gloss":"秘密","context":"There was no secret method that removed all anxiety, only a thought she could test through gradual experience.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"thought","gloss":"想法","context":"There was no secret method that removed all anxiety, only a thought she could test through gradual experience.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"comfort","gloss":"安慰","context":"A friend's comfort helped, but constant reassurance could become a substitute for preparation.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"favor","gloss":"支持","context":"The tutor was in favor of support that made independent action easier.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"ambition","gloss":"抱负","context":"Ambition was valuable when directed toward learning rather than perfect appearances.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"liberal","gloss":"开明的","context":"In a liberal discussion group, students could pause, correct themselves, and ask for clarification.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"quiet","gloss":"安静的","context":"A quiet participant was not necessarily indifferent; mood and confidence varied across settings.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"indifferent","gloss":"冷漠的","context":"A quiet participant was not necessarily indifferent; mood and confidence varied across settings.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"mood","gloss":"心情","context":"A quiet participant was not necessarily indifferent; mood and confidence varied across settings.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"bright","gloss":"聪颖的","context":"One bright classmate with an excellent reputation admitted finding public speaking difficult.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"reputation","gloss":"声誉","context":"One bright classmate with an excellent reputation admitted finding public speaking difficult.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"severe","gloss":"严厉的","context":"The admission challenged the student's severe judgment of herself.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"joy","gloss":"快乐","context":"She began to find joy in understanding an argument and beauty in a clear explanation.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"beauty","gloss":"美","context":"She began to find joy in understanding an argument and beauty in a clear explanation.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"appreciate","gloss":"欣赏","context":"She could appreciate progress without claiming that every rehearsal was successful.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"strict","gloss":"严格的","context":"A strict schedule still mattered, but punishment for every mistake did not make her more eager to improve.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"eager","gloss":"渴望的","context":"A strict schedule still mattered, but punishment for every mistake did not make her more eager to improve.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"surprise","gloss":"惊讶","context":"To her surprise, a short conversation with an audience member sometimes taught more than an hour spent imagining criticism.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"nice","gloss":"好的","context":"It was nice to feel encouraged, yet she became conscious that approval should not determine every choice.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"conscious","gloss":"自觉的","context":"It was nice to feel encouraged, yet she became conscious that approval should not determine every choice.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"spirit","gloss":"精神","context":"A resilient spirit grew from useful habits: resting, preparing, seeking specific feedback, and distinguishing a repairable error from a sweeping judgment about her identity.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"urgent","gloss":"紧急的","context":"On the day of the presentation, an urgent equipment problem caused a moment of alarm.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"alarm","gloss":"恐慌","context":"On the day of the presentation, an urgent equipment problem caused a moment of alarm.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"mystery","gloss":"谜","context":"Confidence was no longer a mystery measured by a perfectly steady voice.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"reluctant","gloss":"不情愿的","context":"The student was reluctant to begin without her slides, then decided to explain the central idea aloud while the technician worked.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":{"en":"reluctant to participate","zh":"不愿参与"}}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"A student preparing her first public speech believed that mental strength meant never feeling uncertain. Her dream was to speak confidently, but practice alone often left her more anxious. She had a strong desire to make her parents happy and held the belief that capable people did not need advice. Every uncomfortable emotion therefore seemed like a moral failure. Her tutor helped her become aware of a different possibility: confidence could include doubt. A smart decision was not necessarily an immediate one, and a calm manner did not reveal how much work had occurred beneath it. The student began to reconsider what competence actually looked like.","zh":"一位准备首次公开讲话的学生认为，心理强大意味着永远不感到不确定。她梦想自信地发言，但独自练习常让她更焦虑。她非常渴望让父母高兴，也相信有能力者不需要建议。因此，每种不舒服情绪都仿佛是道德失败。导师帮助她意识到另一可能：信心可以包含怀疑。聪明决定不一定是立即作出的，平静举止也无法显露背后付出的努力。她开始重新思考，真正的能力是什么样子。"},{"en":"The tutor asked her to begin with a familiar subject rather than demonstrate that she was intelligent through complicated language. The first recording was pretty uneven, but its flaws were useful evidence. Being sensitive to feedback did not mean accepting every criticism as accurate. An introductory lesson in psychology showed how attention could narrow under pressure, regardless of talent. She could maintain a long-term vision while accepting a tough rehearsal. When asked whether she was ready to try again, she answered yes, though she remained afraid. There was no secret method that removed all anxiety, only a thought she could test through gradual experience.","zh":"导师请她从熟悉话题开始，而不是用复杂语言展示聪明。第一段录音相当不稳定，但缺陷是有用证据。对反馈敏感，不等于接受每项批评都准确。一堂心理学入门课说明，压力下注意力可能变窄，与才能无关。她可以保有长期愿景，同时接受艰难的排练。被问及是否准备再试时，她回答“是”，尽管仍害怕。没有消除全部焦虑的秘密方法，只有能通过逐步经历检验的想法。"},{"en":"A friend's comfort helped, but constant reassurance could become a substitute for preparation. The tutor was in favor of support that made independent action easier. Ambition was valuable when directed toward learning rather than perfect appearances. In a liberal discussion group, students could pause, correct themselves, and ask for clarification. A quiet participant was not necessarily indifferent; mood and confidence varied across settings. One bright classmate with an excellent reputation admitted finding public speaking difficult. The admission challenged the student's severe judgment of herself. She realized that other people's polished performance offered incomplete evidence about the struggle, uncertainty, and practice behind it.","zh":"朋友安慰有帮助，但不断寻求保证与安抚可能代替准备。导师支持能够促进独立行动的帮助。抱负指向学习而非完美表象时有价值。在开明讨论小组里，学生可以暂停、自我纠正、请求解释。安静参与者未必冷漠，心情与信心因环境而变。一位聪颖、声誉很好的同学承认公开讲话很困难。这一承认挑战了她对自己的严厉判断。她明白，别人熟练表现并不足以完整说明背后的挣扎、不确定与练习。"},{"en":"She began to find joy in understanding an argument and beauty in a clear explanation. She could appreciate progress without claiming that every rehearsal was successful. A strict schedule still mattered, but punishment for every mistake did not make her more eager to improve. To her surprise, a short conversation with an audience member sometimes taught more than an hour spent imagining criticism. It was nice to feel encouraged, yet she became conscious that approval should not determine every choice. A resilient spirit grew from useful habits: resting, preparing, seeking specific feedback, and distinguishing a repairable error from a sweeping judgment about her identity.","zh":"她开始从理解论证中发现快乐，在清楚解释中发现美。她可以欣赏进步，不必声称每次排练都成功。严格日程仍重要，但对每个错误施罚不会让她更渴望改进。令她惊讶的是，与一位听众短谈，有时比花一小时想象批评更有收获。受鼓励固然很好，但她开始自觉认识到，赞同不应决定每个选择。坚韧精神来自有用习惯：休息、准备、寻求具体反馈，并把可改正错误与对整个自我的笼统评判区分开。"},{"en":"On the day of the presentation, an urgent equipment problem caused a moment of alarm. The student was reluctant to begin without her slides, then decided to explain the central idea aloud while the technician worked. Confidence was no longer a mystery measured by a perfectly steady voice. She could feel nervous and still make a sensible choice. The audience heard a thoughtful argument, including one honest correction. Later, she remembered less about the applause than about that decision to continue. Her achievement was not becoming someone who never needed help, but learning to act with preparation, judgment, and a realistic understanding of her own uncertainty.","zh":"汇报当天，一个紧急设备问题引起片刻恐慌。学生起初不愿在没有幻灯片时开讲，随后决定在技术人员处理设备期间，口头解释核心想法。信心不再是以声音完全平稳来衡量的谜。她可以紧张，同时作出合理选择。听众听到了有思考的论证，其中包括一次诚实纠正。后来，她对掌声的记忆不如对继续讲话的决定鲜明。她的成就不是变成从不需要帮助的人，而是学会凭准备、判断以及对自身不确定性的现实理解来行动。"}],"previous":53,"next":55});
